{"rationale":"1 test_prefix_dp | requirement: each segment is either one literal or a substring of already emitted prefix | technique: direct small-input oracle | oracle: output equals exhaustive prefix DP | validity: recurrence enumerates every legal final segment.
2 test_recursive_segments | requirement: same encoding alternatives | technique: direct oracle | oracle: output equals recursive minimum over legal next segments | validity: every partition is explored.
3 test_backward_dp | requirement: copied text must occur wholly earlier | technique: direct oracle | oracle: exact backward DP value | validity: considers every legal cut.
4 test_partition_search | requirement: concatenation of nonempty encodings | technique: exhaustive enumeration | oracle: minimum enumerated cost | validity: finite complete search.
5 test_edge_relaxation | requirement: literal costs a and references cost b | technique: shortest-path oracle | oracle: shortest prefix path | validity: legal edges exactly match rules.
6 test_all_cuts | requirement: any nonempty substring may be referenced if prior | technique: direct oracle | oracle: minimum over all cuts | validity: no greedy assumption.
7 test_suffix_choices | requirement: references use the preceding produced string | technique: direct oracle | oracle: exact minimum | validity: occurrence is checked only in prefix before cut.
8 test_memo_search | requirement: legal encoding choices | technique: exhaustive recursive oracle | oracle: exact minimum | validity: all valid segment lengths are considered.
9 test_reference_legality | requirement: substring condition | technique: direct oracle | oracle: DP optimum | validity: Python containment directly expresses substring.
10 test_cost_minimum | requirement: print smallest possible number of coins | technique: direct oracle | oracle: equality to computed minimum | validity: optimum is unique numerically. All target the supplied tiny inputs; I would drop test_literal_dp first as redundant.","tests":[{"name":"test_prefix_dp","source":"def test_prefix_dp(run, x):
    first, s = x.strip().splitlines()
    n, a, b = map(int, first.split())
    dp = [0] + [10**18] * n
