{"rationale":"Each test uses the operation definition directly: each leaf-to-leaf path is a vector of edge increments, and arbitrary real configurations are possible exactly when those vectors span all edge coordinates. All supplied trees have n<=8, so exact rational Gaussian elimination is a small direct oracle. 1. test_three_path | requirement: every configuration iff path operations span edges | technique: direct small-input oracle | oracle: YES exactly at full rank | validity: exact for every supplied tree. 2. test_four_path | same requirement/oracle/validity. 3. test_branched_five | same requirement/oracle/validity. 4. test_relabelled_branch | same requirement/oracle/validity. 5. test_mixed_five | same requirement/oracle/validity. 6. test_six_branch | same requirement/oracle/validity. 7. test_binary_seven | same requirement/oracle/validity. 8. test_long_path | same requirement/oracle/validity. 9. test_double_branch | same requirement/oracle/validity. 10. test_irregular_eight | same requirement/oracle/validity. These intentionally independently cover every supplied input despite each oracle being universal; I would drop test_irregular_eight first because it is redundant with the others.","tests":[{"name":"test_three_path","source":"def test_three_path(run, x):
